---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import RelatedWork from '../components/RelatedWork.astro';
import { path } from '../lib/paths';
---
<Layout title="Research — Yucheng Xing" active="research">
  <header class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Research interests</p><h1>Learning through dynamics.</h1><p>My research connects generative modeling, differential equations, and adaptive computation, with applications in computer vision and graph time series.</p></header>
  <div class="research-list">
    <section class="research-section" id="generative">
      <span class="research-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <div><h2>Efficient generative AI</h2><p>I investigate how to control the computation used by diffusion models while retaining useful generative structure. My work explores input-adaptive generation, structured diffusion processes, and conditional image restoration.</p><p>Applications include image generation, rain removal, and forecasting wildfire risk over multiple future horizons.</p><RelatedWork works={[{id:'ac-diff',name:'AC-Diff',venue:'arXiv · 2024'},{id:'spectral-diffusion',name:'Spectral Diffusion',venue:'arXiv · 2026'},{id:'ntree-diffusion',name:'N-Tree Diffusion',venue:'arXiv · 2026'}]} /></div>
      <aside class="research-note"><span class="eyebrow">Current questions</span><p>How much computation does each input need?</p><p>How can the structure of a task inform the generation process?</p></aside>
    </section>
    <section class="research-section" id="adaptive">
      <span class="research-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <div><h2>Adaptive neural architectures</h2><p>I study architectures that adjust computation to the input. Puppet-CNN represents convolutional parameters as a continuous dynamical system, generating layer parameters along a learned trajectory.</p><p>This perspective connects compact model storage with flexible, input-adaptive computation.</p><RelatedWork works={[{id:'puppet-cnn',name:'Puppet-CNN',venue:'ECCV · 2026'}]} /></div>
      <figure class="research-figure"><img src={path('images/puppet-cnn.png')} alt="Puppet-CNN parameter flow and adaptive convolutional architecture" width="320" height="220" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Puppet-CNN: continuous parameter dynamics.</figcaption></figure>
    </section>
    <section class="research-section" id="continuous">
      <span class="research-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <div><h2>Continuous-time neural modeling</h2><p>I use neural differential equations to model motion and graph time series in continuous time. These models provide a natural way to work with irregular observations and evolving relationships.</p><p>My work includes hierarchical human pose forecasting, stochastic prediction on graphs, and unsupervised online denoising.</p><RelatedWork works={[{id:'hdg-ode',name:'HDG-ODE',venue:'ICCV · 2023'},{id:'aggdn',name:'AGGDN',venue:'ICONIP · 2023'},{id:'infinity-net',name:'∞-Net',venue:'ICONIP · 2024'}]} /></div>
      <figure class="research-figure"><img src={path('images/hdg-ode.png')} alt="Hierarchical graph ODE framework for human pose forecasting" width="320" height="200" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>HDG-ODE: hierarchical dynamics for human motion.</figcaption></figure>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style>.research-note{padding:28px;background:var(--wash);border-left:2px solid var(--accent);align-self:center}.research-note p{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:21px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink)}.research-note p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}@media(max-width:720px){.research-note{grid-column:2;padding:22px}.research-note p{font-size:19px}}</style>
